        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1160">

                <pb facs="1050" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/212</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-07T09:00:00+02:30">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1914, 9 a.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Urgent. Austrian Ambassador and staff have left. In view of destruction German
                    Embassy and fearing same Austrian Embassy, am I authorized to raise thereon
                    American flag if I judge it necessary to save Embassy premises and lives of
                    occupants?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
